### TITLE ###
MaxBlocksAnExtraToggle
### DESCRIPTION ###
At the maximum, a further toggle does nothing rather than silently swapping out
an earlier choice.
### PROMPT ###
Pick
### OPTIONS ###
a
b
c
### MAX ###
2
### KEYS ###
space
down
space
down
space
enter
### SELECTED ###
a
b
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
Pick
> [ ] a
  [ ] b
  [ ] c
--- frame 1 (space) ---
Pick
> [x] a
  [ ] b
  [ ] c
--- frame 2 (down) ---
Pick
  [x] a
> [ ] b
  [ ] c
--- frame 3 (space) ---
Pick
  [x] a
> [x] b
  [ ] c
  (max 2 selected)
--- frame 4 (down) ---
Pick
  [x] a
  [x] b
> [ ] c
  (max 2 selected)
--- frame 5 (space) ---
Pick
  [x] a
  [x] b
> [ ] c
  (max 2 selected)
--- frame 6 (enter) ---
Pick a, b

### TITLE ###
MaxReachedHint
### DESCRIPTION ###
Reaching the maximum says so, so a user whose next toggle does nothing can tell
why.
### PROMPT ###
Pick
### OPTIONS ###
a
b
c
### MAX ###
1
### KEYS ###
space
enter
### SELECTED ###
a
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
Pick
> [ ] a
  [ ] b
  [ ] c
--- frame 1 (space) ---
Pick
> [x] a
  [ ] b
  [ ] c
  (max 1 selected)
--- frame 2 (enter) ---
Pick a

### TITLE ###
MinBlocksSubmitAndCountsDown
### DESCRIPTION ###
Enter below the minimum is a no-op, and the frame names how many more are
needed. The second Enter, once the count is met, submits both.
### PROMPT ###
Pick
### OPTIONS ###
a
b
c
### MIN ###
2
### KEYS ###
space
enter
down
space
enter
### SELECTED ###
a
b
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
Pick
> [ ] a
  [ ] b
  [ ] c
  (select 2 more)
--- frame 1 (space) ---
Pick
> [x] a
  [ ] b
  [ ] c
  (select 1 more)
--- frame 2 (enter) ---
Pick
> [x] a
  [ ] b
  [ ] c
  (select 1 more)
--- frame 3 (down) ---
Pick
  [x] a
> [ ] b
  [ ] c
  (select 1 more)
--- frame 4 (space) ---
Pick
  [x] a
> [x] b
  [ ] c
--- frame 5 (enter) ---
Pick a, b
